{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1058079-what-was-the-point-of-the-psychopomps-job","id":1058079,"title":"what was the point of the psychopomps job?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-04T10:29:14-08:00","id":1058079,"title":"what was the point of the psychopomps job?","content":"so..apparently the lack of constant challenge by the avatar was a bad thing.. yet the ixoi found out that&quot; with psychopomps running out they needed to look onto themselves for moral direction&quot;<br /> <br /> also what does&quot;directed the avatars to mages &quot; even means given the setting? people are born with avatars. everyone has one. you don't gain an avatar by awakening it merely well...awakens lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T11:58:32-08:00","id":1058106,"title":"","content":"Due to the appearance of the Entelechy, resonating forward and backward through time, psychopomps manifested.<br /> <br /> People are born with Avatars regardless, but the purpose of the psychopomps was either to specifically guide the proper Avatars to people who would one day Awaken as mages (which, considering they manifested partly because of a Time ripple, might make their job easier) or they generally guided Avatars to all humans, whether or not they'd Awaken.<br /> <br /> Given that, for the purposes of Mage, the specifics of un-Awakened Avatars are generally irrelevant (they're not Awake enough to be able to converse or do magic), it's not inaccurate to just say that psychopomps directed Avatars to mages.<br /> <br /> Psychopomps matched the personalities of the Avatar with the mage so well that the net effect was somewhat counter-productive: the Avatar wanted what the mage wanted, so the Avatar's voice was indistinguishable from the mage's own. Mages forgot they had an Avatar entirely, q.v. the &quot;Fount&quot; in Dark Ages: Mage. As a result, they fell to hubris and the acquisition of mundane power rather than enlightenment.<br /> <br /> By the Renaissance, psychopomps were becoming less frequent, Avatars were left to find their own mages, and as a result were not as well-matched to the mage. They could confront the mage and argue with them, forcing them to question their own decisions. In the case of a strong Avatar, they might drag the mage proverbially kicking and screaming to enlightenment.<br /> <br /> Psychopomps' role was to guide the &quot;right&quot; Avatar to the right person. They were not responsible for the existence of Avatars, merely the proper matching of personalities.<br /> <br /> Think of psychopomps like an optimized dating service: It's their job to find the perfect match. Without a dating service people might still fall in love, and it might be a good match or a bad one, but never the perfect matches the dating service could arrange.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T12:48:19-08:00","id":1058116,"title":"","content":"I thought I saw somewhere on Revised a sidebar saying that the sleeping avatars create the Consensus, so it may not be so useless, but Im not 100% sure, I'll need to check it out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13085-agentsmith","name":"AgentSmith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T13:33:50-08:00","id":1058547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1058079-what-was-the-point-of-the-psychopomps-job?p=1058106#post1058106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Due to the appearance of the Entelechy, resonating forward and backward through time, psychopomps manifested.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is the Entelechy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T06:13:30-08:00","id":1058937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>valismedsen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1058079-what-was-the-point-of-the-psychopomps-job?p=1058547#post1058547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What is the Entelechy?</div> </div> </div> </div>From <b>Ascension</b>: &quot;The Entelechy was the summoning rite prophesied by the Psychopomps. The Khwaja al-Akbar was more than the massed Avatars of the refugees. It was an emanation from the future \u2014 a future when Ascension had been achieved and the Cycle of Creation, including the Sphere of Telos, was realized. But as soon as it touched the imperfect Consensus, it fragmented across the past and future. Partaking of a fraction of the supreme intelligence, these fragments manifested as the Psychopomps who would contact the Ixoi\u2019s ancestors and guide mages for millennia to come.&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200bSo it's a rite that summoned an emanation from an Ascended future. The emanation - the Khwaja al-Akbar - is what gave rise to the Batini.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T06:13:58-08:00","id":1058938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>valismedsen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1058079-what-was-the-point-of-the-psychopomps-job?p=1058547#post1058547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What is the Entelechy?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> basically an ancient entity that was summoned by the batini in the 5 century bc it could not exist in the world however. it shattered and its remnants radiated backwards and forward in time(more or less 2000 years to be precise)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T06:18:09-08:00","id":1058940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1058079-what-was-the-point-of-the-psychopomps-job?p=1058106#post1058106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Due to the appearance of the Entelechy, resonating forward and backward through time, psychopomps manifested.<br /> <br /> People are born with Avatars regardless, but the purpose of the psychopomps was either to specifically guide the proper Avatars to people who would one day Awaken as mages (which, considering they manifested partly because of a Time ripple, might make their job easier) or they generally guided Avatars to all humans, whether or not they'd Awaken.<br /> <br /> Given that, for the purposes of Mage, the specifics of un-Awakened Avatars are generally irrelevant (they're not Awake enough to be able to converse or do magic), it's not inaccurate to just say that psychopomps directed Avatars to mages.<br /> <br /> Psychopomps matched the personalities of the Avatar with the mage so well that the net effect was somewhat counter-productive: the Avatar wanted what the mage wanted, so the Avatar's voice was indistinguishable from the mage's own. Mages forgot they had an Avatar entirely, q.v. the &quot;Fount&quot; in Dark Ages: Mage. As a result, they fell to hubris and the acquisition of mundane power rather than enlightenment.<br /> <br /> By the Renaissance, psychopomps were becoming less frequent, Avatars were left to find their own mages, and as a result were not as well-matched to the mage. They could confront the mage and argue with them, forcing them to question their own decisions. In the case of a strong Avatar, they might drag the mage proverbially kicking and screaming to enlightenment.<br /> <br /> Psychopomps' role was to guide the &quot;right&quot; Avatar to the right person. They were not responsible for the existence of Avatars, merely the proper matching of personalities.<br /> <br /> Think of psychopomps like an optimized dating service: It's their job to find the perfect match. Without a dating service people might still fall in love, and it might be a good match or a bad one, but never the perfect matches the dating service could arrange.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> right i know all that but what does right person mean? my point is,a baby has no personality. unless they are capable of very powerful divination of course. plus people's personas can and do change.<br /> also(while not explicitly stated) it's heavily implied that the stronger the avatar the stronger the propability of awakening anyway. which is why the vast majority of sleepers are said to possess tiny (rating 0) avatars","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-15T17:27:36-07:00","id":1413873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1058079-what-was-the-point-of-the-psychopomps-job#post1058079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so..apparently the lack of constant challenge by the avatar was a bad thing.. yet the ixoi found out that&quot; with psychopomps running out they needed to look onto themselves for moral direction&quot;<br /> <br /> also what does&quot;directed the avatars to mages &quot; even means given the setting? people are born with avatars. everyone has one. you don't gain an avatar by awakening it merely well...awakens lol</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Everyone has an Avatar, but the Avatar does have a distinct nature (defined by Essence and shared experience) and changes across multiple lives, including, in some cases, becoming more likely to Awaken.<br /> <br /> As a mage, you notice your Avatar the most when it's different from you, and when you're in conflict with its desires, which, barring the Cauls, is to seek Ascension. In fact, this conflict *is* the process, via Seeking. If there's no basis for conflict, the Avatar has no reason to make itself known, really, and then you can become an asshole wizard in a tower without hearing any whispers of doubt.<br /> <br /> Yes, this means the psychopomps actually set mages up to fail with a &quot;perfect match&quot; that grants less troubled access to great and terrible power, but doesn't make the noise you need to hear to Ascend. Funny how that sets up the eventual destruction and liberation of all humanity, in a paradox where the &quot;proper matches&quot; produce hubris, and consequent eras of great tribulation. So the psychopomps aren't doing you a favor when they match you. They're fucking with you to do the universe a favor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-30T03:45:30-07:00","id":1450301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malcolm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1058079-what-was-the-point-of-the-psychopomps-job?p=1413873#post1413873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Everyone has an Avatar, but the Avatar does have a distinct nature (defined by Essence and shared experience) and changes across multiple lives, including, in some cases, becoming more likely to Awaken.<br /> <br /> As a mage, you notice your Avatar the most when it's different from you, and when you're in conflict with its desires, which, barring the Cauls, is to seek Ascension. In fact, this conflict *is* the process, via Seeking. If there's no basis for conflict, the Avatar has no reason to make itself known, really, and then you can become an asshole wizard in a tower without hearing any whispers of doubt.<br /> <br /> Yes, this means the psychopomps actually set mages up to fail with a &quot;perfect match&quot; that grants less troubled access to great and terrible power, but doesn't make the noise you need to hear to Ascend. Funny how that sets up the eventual destruction and liberation of all humanity, in a paradox where the &quot;proper matches&quot; produce hubris, and consequent eras of great tribulation. So the psychopomps aren't doing you a favor when they match you. They're fucking with you to do the universe a favor.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> But how does that great and terrible power manifest? Personally, i assumed that it did so with DA mages having a greater capacity to expend/regain <br /> <br /> I like that explanation though. It fits into the idea that a higher being from Beyond is not necessarily your BFF","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}